What is the net effect on the number of elements in a stack after the following sequence of operations? If any elements remain on the stack; what are they? Initial Stack: Empty

**Operations:**

```
Push(10);
Push(20);
Pop();
Push(30);
Pop();
Push(40);
Pop();
Pop();
Push(50);

```

questions.answer:
```c
struct Node *reverse(struct Node *curr) {

    // Base case: If the list is empty or we
    // reach the end of the list 
    if (curr == NULL) return NULL;

    // Swap the next and prev pointers
    struct Node *temp = curr->prev;
    curr->prev = curr->next;
    curr->next = temp;

    // If the previous node (after swap) is NULL
    // this is the new head
    if (curr->prev == NULL) return curr;

    return reverse(curr->prev);
}
```
